==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From late 19th century.  From {{uder|en|grc|ἐρωτικός||related to love}}, which is from {{m|grc|ἔρως||passionate or sexual love}}; {{confix|en|eroto|mania}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|eɪniə|s=6}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A [[disorder]] in which a person has a [[delusion]] of a romantic relationship with another person.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Megan Nolan|title=Acts of Desperation|year=2021|publisher=Random House|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=BjDhDwAAQBAJ&hl=&=onepage&q&f=false|isbn=978-1-4735-7850-0|passage=I read a case study of a woman, Patient M, who suffered from '''erotomania''', or De Clerambault syndrome, in upstate New York in the 1970s. {{...}} One July morning, professional acquaintances and friends of the professor were shocked tor receive wedding invitations to the marriage of him and Patient M.}}
# Excessive sexual [[inclination]] or [[desire]].

